DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     mmaann locates and prints the manual page for each _t_i_t_l_e named
     on the command line.  Pages live below /uussrr/mmaann. By default
     mmaann searches both the command and the system sections and
     displays the pre-formatted copy of the page through ssccaatt.

     The section flags may be combined; when both are given (the
     default), each _t_i_t_l_e is looked for in the command section
     first and then the system section.

     -cc   Look only in the command section.

     -ss   Look only in the system section.

     -nn   Re-format the page: run its unformatted source through
          nnrrooffff -mmaann and pipe the result through ssccaatt. Any option
          beginning with - other than those listed here is passed
          on to nnrrooffff unchanged.

     -ww   Do not display the page; print only the path of the
          file in which the document resides.

     If a _t_i_t_l_e is not found, mmaann reports whether it was missing
     from the command section, the system section, or the manual
     as a whole.

